/-!
# `Work.MotAS.ASZPhi` — the chart of the linear projection `F = phiAS a b`

The forward link map of the AS branch is the **linear** projection
`F = phiAS a b : ℙ⁴_Y ⇢ ℙ³_X`, `X_{j-1} = (F Y)_j / (F Y)_0`, and it carries the AS-twisted Klein
curve `C_{3·fAS} = V(kleinPAS a b (3·fAS))` into the residual curve `C' = V(ZIAS a b fAS)` of the
AS quadro-cubic link (session 2026-10-06, `STATUS_ASZTwistDivPlaneGeom.md`; the ideal-level
containment is `Work.MotAS.asPhi_mem`).

This module only carries the *definition* of the resulting chart map
`asPhi D : K[x₀,x₁,x₂] →ₐ[K] ↥(twistFieldAS D (3 * fAS 𝕜))` (`K = RatFunc 𝕜`), so that the two
remaining (independent) facts about it can be proved in parallel in separate modules:

* `RingHom.ker (asPhi D) = √(ZIAS (aK D) (bK D) (fAS 𝕜))` — the residual curve is a *curve*, i.e.
  the projection is dominant and birational onto its image;
* `Subfield.closure (K ∪ range (asPhi D)) = ⊤` — the chart map generates the twist field.

## The generation statement `Subfield.closure (K ∪ range (asPhi D)) = ⊤` — direct route

This one needs **no** certificate either.  Put `ỹ := asTwY D (3 • fAS 𝕜)` (so `ỹ₀ ≠ 0`) and
`ρ_k := ỹ_k/ỹ₀` for `k = 0,…,4` (so `ρ₀ = 1`); these are the chart coordinates of the twisted
Klein curve, and `↥(twistFieldAS D (3 • fAS 𝕜)) = K(ρ₁,ρ₂,ρ₃,ρ₄) = K(ρ₁,…,ρ₄)`.  The direct
computation

  `asPhi D (X_i) = (F ỹ)_{i+1}/(F ỹ)₀`  and (using `kleinPAS1 a b (3·fAS) ỹ = 0`)
  `(3a+b)ρ₁ + (3a+4b)ρ₃ = 1`

gives, after inverting the (explicit, triangular) linear system `(F Y)_j = (F Y)₀·X_{j-1}`,

  `ρ_k = P_k(asPhi D (X 0), asPhi D (X 1), asPhi D (X 2)) / Q(asPhi D (X 0), …)`  for `k = 1,…,4`

with `Q` an explicit polynomial in the three images.  Hence every `ρ_k` lies in
`Subfield.closure (K ∪ range (asPhi D))`, and so does the whole twist field.  (Equivalently: the
subfield generated by the three images contains the `ρ_k`, whose mutual ratios generate
`↥(twistFieldAS D (3 • fAS 𝕜))`.)

## The explicit inverse (the route to the kernel statement)

On the chart `Y₀ = 1` of `C_{3·fAS}`, the linear equations `(F Y)_j = (F Y)_0 · X_{j-1}` solve
for `(Y₁,Y₂,Y₃,Y₄)` linearly in `(X₀,X₁,X₂)`:

* `Y₃ = X₁/(a+2b)`, `Y₄ = X₂/(4a+3b)`,
* `Y₁ = (1 - (3a+4b)·X₁/(a+2b))/(3a+b)`,
* `Y₂ = (X₀ - (a+3b)·X₂/(4a+3b))/(3a+b)`,

and `Y₀` is then determined by the single Pfaffian equation that is *linear* in `Y₀`, namely
`kleinPAS1 a b (3·fAS)`.  The resulting `ρ` satisfies the identity `Φ(ρ_k) = Y_k/(F Y)_0` on
`C_{3·fAS}` (`k = 0,…,4`), whence the `K`-algebra map `Y_j ↦ ρ_j/ρ_0` is a left inverse of `asPhi`
on the level of rings — which yields the kernel statement once the one remaining *polynomial*
certificate `kleinPAS_j a b (3·fAS) ρ ∈ √(ZIAS a b fAS)` (verified numerically over all admissible
`(a,b,g) ∈ 𝔽₅³`) is available.

The concrete certificate is recorded in `Submission/Work/MotAS/STATUS_ASZTwistDivPlaneGeom_S7.md`.

## The *easy* half of the kernel statement: `√ZIAS ≤ ker (asPhi D)`

This half needs **no** certificate, and the route is:

1. `RingHom.ker (asPhi D)` is prime (a kernel into the field `↥(twistFieldAS …)`), hence radical;
   so it suffices to show `ZIAS ≤ ker (asPhi D)`, for which it suffices to show
   `asPhi D (zcubAS (aK D) (bK D) (fAS 𝕜) k) = 0` for each `k : Fin 5`.
2. `zcubAS a b g k = kleinRAS (C a) (C b) (C g) ![1, X 0, X 1, X 2, 0] k` (definitional), so
   `asPhi D (zcubAS … k) = kleinRAS a b g ![1, ΦX₀, ΦX₁, ΦX₂, 0] k` where `ΦXᵢ = asPhi D (X i)`
   and `a, b, g` are the images in the twist field (an `aeval` computation: unfold `kleinRAS` and
   push `aeval` through `+ * ^`, using `aeval_X`/`aeval_C`).
3. Writing `ỹ := asTwY D (3 • fAS 𝕜)` (so `ΦXᵢ = ỹ_{i+1}/ỹ₀` by definition of `asChartPhi`), one has
   `![1, ΦX₀, ΦX₁, ΦX₂, 0] = ỹ₀⁻¹ • (F ỹ)` — because `phiAS k 0 = 0` for every `k` and
   `(F ỹ)₄ = 0`.
4. `kleinRAS a b g` is homogeneous of degree `3`, so
   `kleinRAS ![1,ΦX₀,ΦX₁,ΦX₂,0] k = ỹ₀⁻³ · kleinRAS (F ỹ) k`, and
   `kleinRAS (F ỹ) k ∈ (kleinPAS a b (3*g) ỹ)` by `Work.MotAS.asPhi_mem`
   (`Submission/Work/MotAS/asPhi_mem.lean`, proved), whose generators all vanish at `ỹ`
   (`Work.MotAS.kleinPAS_asTwY`, proved in `ASZChartSetup.lean`).
   Hence `asPhi D (zcubAS … k) = 0`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

namespace Work.MotAS

open MvPolynomial

variable {𝕜 : Type} [Field 𝕜] [CharP 𝕜 5]

/-- The five linear forms `(F Y)_k = Σ_j phiAS a b k j · Y_j` of the forward link map `F = phiAS`,
as elements of `K[Y₀,…,Y₄]`.  Note `phiAS a b k 0 = 0` for every `k`, so these do not involve
`Y₀` at all. -/
noncomputable def asFY (a b : RatFunc 𝕜) (k : Fin 5) : MvPolynomial (Fin 5) (RatFunc 𝕜) :=
  ∑ j : Fin 5, MvPolynomial.C (phiAS a b k j) * MvPolynomial.X j

/-- **The chart of the linear projection** `F = phiAS a b`, i.e. the `K`-algebra map
`K[X₀,X₁,X₂] →ₐ[K] ↥(twistFieldAS D (3 * fAS 𝕜))`, `X_{j-1} ↦ (F Y)_j/(F Y)_0`, evaluated at the
chart `Y₀ = 1` of the AS-twisted Klein curve of class `3 * fAS 𝕜`. -/
noncomputable def asPhi (D : Work.MotV.KleinData 𝕜) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin 3) (RatFunc 𝕜) →ₐ[RatFunc 𝕜]
      ↥(twistFieldAS D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜)) :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval ![
    asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 1)
      / asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 0),
    asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 2)
      / asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 0),
    asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 3)
      / asChartPhi D (3 • Work.MotV.fAS 𝕜) (asFY (aK D) (bK D) 0)]

end Work.MotAS
